   "1:4": {
    "u": "https://phish.in/2026-04-25/axilla-part-ii",
    "d": 1056,
    "tags": [
     {
      "name": "Alt Lyric",
      "notes": "Trey used alternate lyrics that referenced the visuals, saying, \"Don't shine that hot dog in my face...grind it, grind it...\""
     },
     {
      "name": "Jamcharts",
      "notes": "After warning some hot dogs to get out of his face, Trey is primed and ready to take Axilla deep again. The band is comfortable hanging in the murk of the song and doesn't rush towards any of their \"comfort jamming zones.\" The jam feels gooey as it oozes along. Those who don't need their jams to peak should seek this out. > into \"Cities\"."
     }
    ]
   },
   "1:5": {
    "u": "https://phish.in/2026-04-25/cities",
    "d": 1001,
    "tags": [
     {
      "name": "Jamcharts",
      "notes": "Cosmopolitan jam that stays fairly close to home rhythmically but departs melodically under Trey's lead, brightening and decorating the neighborhood with a brisk and buoyant optimism and a gentle uplift before returning to the song to conclude."
     }
    ]
   },
   "1:6": {
